Python:
Python is usually considered an interpreted language. 
When we run a Python program, the Python interpreter handles the code and executes it. 
Python first converts the code into bytecode, which is then run by the Python Virtual Machine.

C:
C is a compiled language. 
Before running a C program, a compiler converts the entire program into machine code that the computer can understand. 
After compilation, the generated executable file can be run.

Java:
Java works a little differently. 
First, the Java compiler converts the source code into bytecode. 
This bytecode is then executed by the Java Virtual Machine (JVM).
